{"title":"Career Roadmap · Biopharma Executive","role":"Biopharma Executive","summary":"A Biopharma Executive works in the biotechnology and pharmaceutical industry across areas such as biological products, vaccines, therapeutics, microbiology, quality, manufacturing, regulatory operations, clinical research, product support and commercial operations.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starting point"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Biotechnology / Microbiology / Life Sciences"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Immunology / Virology / Industrial Microbiology"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Biopharma Executive"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Biotechnology · Biopharmaceuticals · Vaccines · Life Sciences"}],[{"text":"Main industry areas"},{"text":"R&D · Manufacturing · QC · QA · Regulatory · Clinical Research · Commercial"}],[{"text":"Core capability"},{"text":"Biological science + regulated industry operations"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build microbiology, immunology, virology, bioprocess and industry fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Choose QC, QA, manufacturing, clinical research, regulatory, R&D or commercial operations"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Move toward specialist, senior executive or managerial responsibilities"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine biopharma expertise with automation, data, AI, regulatory technology and advanced biologics"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc graduate specialising in Immunology, Virology or Industrial Microbiology, the strongest entry routes are generally biopharma trainee, QC/QA, manufacturing, laboratory, clinical research or technical-support roles, followed by progression 